From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb_wifi: auto-connect immediately after successful pairing

After pairing succeeds, the device switches from the pairing port to a connect
port and advertises _adb-tls-connect._tcp. But mDNS discovery may take 5-15
seconds to detect the new service, leaving the user waiting. Restore the
immediate post-pair auto-connect call (adb_secure_connect_by_service_name)
that was removed in patch 0014, but defer it to the MAIN fdevent thread via
fdevent_run_on_main_thread to avoid the cross-thread data race:

  - pair_service runs on its own SERVICE thread (create_service_thread)
  - adb_secure_connect_by_service_name reads sAdbSecureConnectServices
  - that registry is mutated (push_back/erase) by discovery callbacks on the
    MAIN fdevent thread
  - reading it from the pair thread without a lock is UB (concurrent
    push_back can reallocate, invalidating iterators)

Deferring to main thread sidesteps the race: the connect runs on the same
thread that owns the registry. The lambda captures device_guid by value so
it remains valid after adb_wifi_pair_device returns.

Aiden-local patch (immediate post-pair auto-connect, thread-safe).
---
--- a/vendor/core/adb/client/adb_wifi.cpp
+++ b/vendor/core/adb/client/adb_wifi.cpp
@@ -267,5 +267,20 @@
 
     // Write to adb_known_hosts
     write_known_host_to_file(device_guid);
-    // Try to auto-connect.
+
+    // Try to auto-connect immediately after pairing. The device will switch from
+    // the pairing port to a connect port and advertise _adb-tls-connect, but mDNS
+    // discovery may take 5-15 seconds to see it. Trigger an immediate connect by
+    // service name (the GUID we just received) to avoid the user waiting.
+    //
+    // IMPORTANT: adb_secure_connect_by_service_name() reads sAdbSecureConnectServices,
+    // which is mutated by discovery callbacks on the MAIN fdevent thread. We're
+    // currently on the pair SERVICE thread (create_service_thread). Reading that
+    // vector without a lock is a data race (concurrent push_back during discovery
+    // can reallocate the vector, invalidating our iterator). Solution: defer the
+    // connect call to the main thread via fdevent_run_on_main_thread, so it runs
+    // on the same thread that mutates the registries.
+    fdevent_run_on_main_thread([device_guid]() {
+        adb_secure_connect_by_service_name(device_guid.c_str());
+    });
 }
